# Secrets — never let these end up in a build context/image layer, even if
# a future Dockerfile change ever does something broader than today's
# targeted `COPY backend/ ./backend/` + `COPY frontend/ .` (neither touches
# root .env today, but this is the explicit guarantee, not an accident of
# directory layout).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Runtime data / secrets-adjacent — never baked into the image, always
# mounted as volumes (see docker-compose.yml) or written at runtime.
# Every path below is checked against what actually writes it, not
# guessed from the docker-compose mount alone — the file the code writes
# and the path the mount targets aren't always the same:
#   - data/          SQLALCHEMY_DATABASE_URI + uploads (app.py), ./data mount.
#   - backend/logs/  audit_log()'s AUDIT_LOG_DIR (app.py) is backend/logs/,
#                    not the top-level logs/ the web container bind-mounts
#                    it to (docker-compose.yml) — both are real, on-disk
#                    paths; excluding only one leaves the other exposed.
#   - backup/*.db    POST /api/backup (trigger_backup, app.py) writes
#                    backup/chantier_<timestamp>.db directly — flat, .db.
#                    NOT backup/**/*.zip (the pattern this used to be):
#                    wrong extension, and implies nesting that isn't there
#                    — it never matched an actual file.
#   - backups/       the separate "backup" cron service's monthly dump
#                    (backup/backup.sh -> *.zip), host-mounted at
#                    ./backups — a different directory than backup/ above,
#                    easy to conflate by name alone.
data/
logs/
backend/logs/
backup/*.db
backups/
*.log

# Dev/VCS noise irrelevant to the image. .git with no trailing slash (not
# .git/) matches both a real .git/ directory (a normal clone) AND the
# single-file gitdir pointer a git worktree checkout has instead (this repo
# is checked out as a worktree, confirmed on disk: .git here is a 95-byte
# text file, not a directory) — a directory-only pattern silently misses
# the file case.
.git
**/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
dist/
